                "end_index": 612,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Indirect Causes (Bone and Muscle Pain)\nThe most common way parathyroid disease causes neck pain is not from the gland itself, but from how the disease affects your bones and muscles:\n* **Cervical Spine Bone Pain:** Hyperparathyroidism causes the body to produce too much parathyroid hormone (PTH)"
